From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 03:01:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] amsi: scan with the host's scanner instead of answering
 "nothing detected".

Office asks AMSI to look at a macro before it runs it, and asks for the
Antimalware class by CLSID to do so.  The stub answered every scan with
AMSI_RESULT_NOT_DETECTED and had no class at all, which is the worst of
both: an application that does get an answer is entitled to believe
something examined the content, and one that cannot create the class
treats it as a scan it could not perform and refuses the macro outright.

Put a real scanner behind it.  The unix side speaks clamd's INSTREAM
protocol over its local socket -- found from WINE_AMSI_CLAMD_SOCKET, then
clamd's own configuration, then the paths distributions use -- and reports
what the engine actually said.

Nothing here may turn "could not scan" into "clean".  With no scanner
reachable AmsiInitialize and the class factory both fail, so the caller
learns it has no scanning available rather than being handed a verdict
that means nothing; a connection that drops, a size limit, or a protocol
error likewise comes back as a failure with the verdict untouched.
Handles come from the caller, so validating them is guarded against being
given something that was never ours.

Word reaches this as OFFICE_VBA and the scanner answers: the EICAR test
string comes back DETECTED and ordinary macro text NOT_DETECTED, over both
the flat API and the COM surface.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 79ff09dcc41bfcde6a309e8ec656f6539cf1f3d1)

